<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patiala and East Punjab States Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948–1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as PEPSU</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Patiala and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-punjab">East Punjab</a> States Union was a state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> formed in 1948 by merging eight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, including Patiala, Nabha, Jind, Kapurthala, Faridkot, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malerkotla">Malerkotla</a> and Kalsia, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Patiala as its head. Its capital was Patiala. In 1956 it was merged into the state of Punjab.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patiala-and-east-punjab-states-union.jpg" alt="Patiala and East Punjab States Union" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: India 1951 Bombay.svg: Superbenjamin this file: Furfur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PEPSU_in_India_(1951).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
